cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CEQA Preflight, please cite it as below."
title: "CEQA Preflight"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kelly-Reif"
    given-names: "Chelsea"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ChelseaKR/ceqa-preflight"
license: "Apache-2.0"
# `version` mirrors pyproject.toml (single source of truth); tests/test_release_claims.py
# asserts the two agree.
#
# `date-released` is absent, and has been wrong in both directions. It first carried
# 2026-07-18, the first commit date, which is not a release. It then carried 2026-09-02,
# described here as "the date of the v0.1.0 tag" -- and no v0.1.0 tag was ever cut:
# `git tag --list` is empty and the repository has no GitHub Release. Citation tooling
# prints this field as the date the software was released, so both times the file
# published a release date for a release that did not exist.
#
# The check that was supposed to prevent that read a heading in CHANGELOG.md, and both
# files were edited in the same commit, so a document agreed with a document while both
# stopped being true. tests/test_release_claims.py ties this field to `git tag --list`
# instead, in both directions: it may not appear without a tag naming the declared
# version, and it may not be missing once one exists.
version: "0.1.0"
abstract: "A local, source-cited advisory preflight checker for CEQA Submit filing packages."
